WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.534
[ Claps ]

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:04.634
Everybody!

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:05.667
[ Claps ]

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.567
Welcome back
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:08.601
[ Claps ]

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.567
We love songs.
[ Claps ]

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.934
We especially love songs
written by our audience members.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:13.934
[ Claps ]

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.100
In under an hour.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.267
[ Claps ]
Ah, gotcha!

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.334
It's time for "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.100
Here we go!

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.667
-♪ Writing a song
and singing the song ♪

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.501
♪ And writing a song
about another song ♪

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.300
-Welcome to "Battle of the
Instant Songwriters."

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.968
Before the show,
we went through our audience

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.667
and we picked out two people who
said that they were musicians.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.901
And we gave them each
made up a so--

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.968
a made-up song title
to each of them -- okay? --

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.133
and gave them one hour
to write an original song

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.667
based on that title.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.567
Here's a shot of them practicing
backstage a minute ago.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.467
This is real.
Yeah.

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:47.801
Let's see
what they come up with.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.634
Let's meet our contestants.
Come on over, everyone.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.767
Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:54.367
Nice to see you.
How are you?

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:57.367
Hey, nice to see you, bud.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.934
Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:00.434
-Let's start
with contestant number one.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:02.100
What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.300
-My name's from Katie Martucci.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.634
I'm from West Hurley, New York.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.534
-West Hurley, New York!
Come on!

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:08.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.634
Shout-out to Dottie and Tommy.
I love West Hurley, New York.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.601
What is the title of the song
that you were given?

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:17.334
-My song is called "Filled my
Hot Tub with Pumpkin Spice."

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.667
-Ah, we gave you
a good one there.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.901
Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.234
-What instrument will you be
playing tonight?

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.834
-The guitar.
-Oh. Well, please,

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.000
go get ready on stage.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.801
Thank you very much
for being here, Katie.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:32.767
Katie, this is very exciting.

00:01:32.767 --> 00:01:35.000
And now, ladies and gentlemen,
here to perform

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.667
the world premiere
of the soon-to-be-classic

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.234
"Filled my Hot Tub
with Pumpkin Spice,"

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.400
it's Katie Martucci.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:50.100
♪♪

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.267
-♪ Feel the crisp in the air ♪

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:56.334
♪ Summer's come to an end,
and it's time to prepare ♪

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:59.567
♪ Got my sweater, got my plaid ♪

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.334
♪ Just one thing
that I'm missing ♪

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:02.634
♪ And it's driving me mad ♪

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.100
♪ I want someone ♪

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.868
♪ I want you ♪

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:08.567
♪ And I think I know
just what to do ♪

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.334
♪ Don't go to Starbucks ♪

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.901
♪ Come to mine ♪

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:19.467
♪ 'Cause I fill my hot tub
with pumpkin spice ♪

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:25.501
♪ Why do you look
so surprised? ♪

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:29.534
♪ You know it's gonna be
so nice ♪

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.634
♪ Sweeter than pie ♪

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:37.000
♪ So come soak with me
under the leaves ♪

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.367
♪ Bubbles between you and I ♪

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:44.133
♪ Pumpkin spice ♪

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.567
♪ You and I ♪

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:49.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.334
-Wow!
That's actually...

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.033
Katie Martucci!

00:02:55.033 --> 00:02:56.667
That was incredible.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.167
Oh, you made it sound beautiful.

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.801
How'd you do that?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.334
-That's almost impossible to do.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.434
All right.
Uh, good luck.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:06.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.167
Contestant number two,

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:08.334
what is your name,
and where are you from?

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:09.567
-My name is Sean McVerry.

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:10.767
I'm from Middlebury,
Connecticut.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.868
-Yeah, Sean McVerry!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.634
Middlebury, Connecticut.

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:18.200
Sean, tell everybody
what your song title is.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.200
-My song is called

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.434
"Fantasy Football,
Regular Life."

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.234
-What instrument
will you be playing tonight?

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:26.300
-I'm playing the piano.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.367
-Sean, take the stage
and get ready.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.334
Get prepared.
This is an experience.

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.100
Get in the zone.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.467
Channel that inspiration, Sean.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.000
Ladies and gentlemen,
get ready for the world premiere

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:42.834
of "Fantasy Football,
Regular Life," by Sean McVerry.

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.400
♪♪

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.300
-♪ I've got Aaron Rogers ♪

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.734
♪ As my first-round pick ♪

00:03:55.734 --> 00:04:00.767
♪ Hanging in my apartment
with my roommate Rick ♪

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:02.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:05.133
♪ I catch a pizza bagel
in my mouth ♪

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:09.367
♪ And I get a high-five ♪

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:14.667
♪ Fantasy football,
regular life ♪

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:17.767
♪ High stakes
at the Sunday games ♪

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:21.067
♪ In these players
I place my trust ♪

00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:24.300
♪ A quarterback back
in the prime of his life ♪

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.067
♪ And I come to
covered in Dorito dust ♪

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:32.434
♪ Sometimes I wonder if ♪

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.400
♪ They'd ever switch places
with me ♪

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.868
♪ Probably not, definitely not ♪

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:42.033
♪ But a boy's got to dream ♪

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:45.567
♪ Until then,
I focus on my draft ♪

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:49.868
♪ And I'll have a good time ♪

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:56.501
♪ Fantasy football,
regular life ♪

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:59.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:01.300
-Yo!

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.000
Are you kidding me?!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.234
Well done.
-Thank you very much.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.801
-Sean McVerry!

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:09.467
Both of you.
Oh, my God!

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.200
Well done!
That was awesome.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.367
That might be the best one
we've done yet.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.267
Now it's time to see who won.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:18.467
We're gonna let our great
audience decide the winner.

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:20.167
[ Audience boos ]

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.300
Unbelievable, you guys.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:28.667
I enjoyed both, of course,
but there can only be one.

00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:30.534
Was it Katie Martucci?

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:33.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.901
Or was it Sean McVerry?

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:36.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:39.267
Sean McVerry!
Congratulations!

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.434
You are the winner!

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:43.801
Sean McVerry,
you will be going home

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:46.334
with a "I Love Music"
sweatshirt.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:47.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.567
Congratulations.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:54.767
-Also, you'll be going home
with a Samsung Galaxy Book2 Pro

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:58.067
to write and record more songs.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:05:59.767
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you very much.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:03.834
-You got that hot tub.
-Yeah.

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:05.701
-No.
No one goes home empty-handed.

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.000
Of course,
our other contestant will get

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.734
an "I Love Music" sweatshirt,
as well.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.501
-Yay!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:15.033
-And we're gonna give you
the Samsung Galaxy Book2 Pro.

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:17.601
Thank you so much.
Both, amazing jobs.

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:20.634
Give it up for your two new
instant songwriters!

